# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mingjie Wen et al. (2025). EMFF-2025: a general neural network potential for energetic materials with C, H, N, and O elements.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-025-01809-w
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 8f9412d1ac37c660...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 529 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wen2025emff.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the EMFF-2025 DeePMD model for 20 high-energy
# materials, developed from the authors' pre-trained DP-CHNO-2024 by 45
# DP-GEN iterations (6,900 new configurations) on top of a 27,000-
# configuration PBE-D3 base dataset for RDX, HMX and CL-20; the overall
# and per-material MAEs stated for the training data. Iteration-by-
# iteration stability/extrapolation MAEs, cell parameters, EOS and
# decomposition results are not encoded as results.

